beer_hagolah.en:
There, law 3, from the Mishnah in HaSho'el, Bava Metzia 98b: the borrower said, 'send it to me through my son,' etc.<br>
The Mishnah's use of 'his son' implies even a minor, because an adult son would simply be his agent. It is also learned from the nearby rule that handing a flask to a minor is considered intentional abandonment, etc.<br>
And I'm going to say, &quot;I'm going to give you.&quot;
